    "facts": "Hennur Police has filed chargesheet against the accused for the offences punishable under sec.498A,\n306 of Indian Penal Code.\nThe deceased is the legally wedded wife of the accused and their marriage was solemnized on 08.07.2012.\nThe accused demanded and received cash of Rs.2,50,000/- and gold worth Rs.1,50,000/- as  3 S.C.No.714/2019 dowry.\nAfter marriage, the husband and wife were residing at Benson Town.\nShe gave birth to male child.\nLater, the accused had developed illicit relationship,\nneglected the deceased and treated her with physical and mental cruelty.\nHe used to consume alcohol and demanded divorce.\nSo, the deceased was residing with her parents.\nThe accused had sent divorce notice to the deceased.\nWithout bearing the torture and cruelty,\non 12.12.2017, she hanged herself and committed suicide.\nThe accused had instigated and abetted his wife to commit suicide.\n",
    "issue": "8. The points that arise for my consideration are:\n 1.\nWhether the prosecution proves beyond all reasonable doubt that the accused married the deceased on 08.07.2012, residing at Benson Town, later developed extra marital affair, treated the deceased with cruelty, neglected to maintain her, issued divorce notice and thereby committed the offence punishable under sec.498A of IPC?\n2.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "There are no cogent evidence to establish that the accused had instigated and abetted the deceased to commit suicide.\n15. It is settled law that in case of alleged abetment of suicide, there must be a proof of direct or indirect act of incitement to the commission of suicide.\nMere allegation of harassment of the deceased would not sufficient unless there be such action on the part of the accused which compels the person to commit suicide.\nInstigation means to provoke, incite or encourage to do an act.\nThere are no cogent evidence to establish that the accused has treated his wife with cruelty and she was subjected to harassment.\nFurther, there is no evidence to establish the accused had abetted and instigated her to commit suicide.\n",
